#X obj 60 1046 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets\ and\ outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1074 Inlet: messages (see Messages) \; Outlet 0 \, 1: signal left / right (~55.9 kHz resampled) \; Outlet 2: lcd \, led \, midiout \, info \, voice \, channel \, \;   voicedata, f 64;
#X obj 60 1166 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1194 note <p> <v> [ch] \, cc <n> <v> [ch] \, pgm <n> [ch] \, \;   bend <-8192..8191> [ch]: MIDI to the TX81Z \; <float> / list \, midi <bytes>: raw MIDI bytes ([midiin]) \; <name> <value>: a voice parameter \, TX81Z data value \, \;   e.g. alg 4 \, out1 99 (all names: Voice parameters) \; n <name> <0-127>: the same from a pot / CC position \; ninfo <name>: outlet 2 gets info <name> <0-127> <value> \, \;   every change is reported this way by itself \; vced <p> <d> \, aced <p> <d>: raw parameter change \; dumpreq: ask the firmware for the edit buffer (also \;   done by itself after every program change) \; channel <0-16>: receive channel of the TX81Z \, 0 = omni. \;   note \, cc \, pgm \, bend without [ch] and SysEx follow it \; getvoice: outlet 2 gets voicedata <name> <93 VCED> \;   <23 ACED> \, voicedata ...: that voice into the edit \;   buffer (bulk dump) \, as the editor's user bank does \; press <button> \, button <button> 0/1: front panel \; rom <file> \, nvram <file> \, save \, reset: firmware and \;   battery RAM (saved on save and when the patch closes) \; factoryinit: presets \, MIDI setup \, program change on \;   (runs by itself if the nvram file does not exist yet) \; pcswitch 0/1/2 \, sysparam <p> <d>: system setup \; gain <f>: output gain (default 1), f 64;
#X obj 60 1590 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Editor\ (txedit) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1618 [txedit \$0-tx81z] above: click it to open the editor. All 100 voice parameters in rows of 8: rows 1-11 are the CC pages of the controller layer \, then two rows without CC. Each cell: name and CC number \, slider and number box 0-127 (n <name> <value>) and the value as on the TX81Z. On top: voice name \, program change (bank + patch) \, the LCD \, the MIDI channel (receive channel of the TX81Z \, 0 = omni: notes \, controller layer and SysEx follow it) and the user bank: 64 slots in txuser-bank.txt next to the editor. user N loads slot N \, store to N chooses a slot and save patch saves the current voice there and writes the file \, load bank reads it again. factory init: factory voices in bank I and the factory setup. A program change in EDIT mode first presses PLAY (the firmware ignores program changes while editing). To keep a voice in the TX81Z itself: STORE on the front panel. \; It sends to the bus and reads outlet 2 from the -out bus: tx81z~ reports every change there (info) \, so the controller \, program changes and messages show up in it. In your own patch: [txedit <name>] next to [r <name>] -> [tx81z~] -> outlet 2 -> [s <name>-out]., f 64;
#X obj 60 1966 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MIDI\ CC:\ controller\ layer\ (txcc) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1994 [txcc 2] above is the controller layer of tx81z~ (the same as p8cc of pdoly8~): MIDI CC on the instrument's channel -> n <name> <value> onto the bus. The argument (2) is the channel until tx81z~ reports its receive channel (channel <n> on outlet 2 \, set in the editor or with the channel message): then [txcc] follows it \, 0 = omni = all channels. Every instrument has its own channel and the same CC pages \, so the controller keeps one setup: page k = row k in the editor. \; Pages: 20-119 without 32 \, 38 \, 64-69 \, 84 \, 88 \, 96-101. \; Changes from elsewhere (program change \, editor \, messages) go back to the controller as CC on the same channel and number. Pickup: after such a change an encoder acts only when it reaches the value or crosses it (pickup 0 turns that off). CC 3 or sync sends all values to the controller. \; page 1 VOICE \, CC 20-27: alg fb out1 out2 out3 out4 trps rev \; page 2 OP1 \, CC 28-31 33-36: crs1 fin1 osw1 ar1 d1r1 d1l1 d2r1 rr1 \; page 3 OP2 \, CC 37 39-45: crs2 fin2 osw2 ar2 d1r2 d1l2 d2r2 rr2 \; page 4 OP3 \, CC 46-53: crs3 fin3 osw3 ar3 d1r3 d1l3 d2r3 rr3 \; page 5 OP4 \, CC 54-61: crs4 fin4 osw4 ar4 d1r4 d1l4 d2r4 rr4 \; page 6 DETUNE / VELOCITY \, CC 62-63 70-75: det1 det2 det3 det4 kvs1 kvs2 kvs3 kvs4 \; page 7 LFO \, CC 76-83: lfw lfs lfd pmd amd pms ams sync \; page 8 SCALING \, CC 85-87 89-93: rs1 rs2 rs3 rs4 ls1 ls2 ls3 ls4 \; page 9 FIXED / AM \, CC 94-95 102-107: fix1 fix2 fix3 fix4 ame1 ame2 ame3 ame4 \; page 10 EG SHIFT / BIAS \, CC 108-115: sh1 sh2 sh3 sh4 ebs1 ebs2 ebs3 ebs4 \; page 11 CONTROLLERS \, CC 116-119: pbr port mwp mwa \; A parameter change is sent to the firmware as SysEx (7 bytes \, about 2 ms at 31250 baud). tx81z~ sends only the newest value of each parameter and only while its MIDI input is idle \, so notes are never delayed by a turning knob. The steps themselves are the firmware's (e.g. 100 output levels): a fast sweep can sound stepped \, as on the real TX81Z., f 64;
#X obj 60 2598 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (example\ parameters) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2626 alg (0): algorithm 0-7 (shown as 1-8 on the TX81Z). \; fb (0): feedback of operator 4 \, 0-7. \; out1 (99): output level of operator 1 \, 0-99. \; out2 (0): output level of operator 2 \, 0-99. \; out3 (0): output level of operator 3 \, 0-99. \; out4 (0): output level of operator 4 \, 0-99. \; lfs (35): LFO speed \, 0-99. \; pmd (0): pitch modulation depth of the LFO \, 0-99., f 64;
#X obj 60 2782 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Voice\ parameters 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2810 Voice (data values as stored in the TX81Z): \; alg 0-7: algorithm (1-8 on the TX81Z) \; fb 0-7: feedback of operator 4 \; lfs 0-99: lfo speed \; lfd 0-99: lfo delay \; pmd 0-99: pitch modulation depth \; amd 0-99: amplitude modulation depth \; sync 0-1: LFO key sync \; lfw 0-3: LFO wave: saw square triangle S/H \; pms 0-7: pitch modulation sensitivity \; ams 0-3: amplitude modulation sensitivity \; trps 0-48: transpose (24 = middle C) \; poly 0-1: poly / mono \; pbr 0-12: pitch bend range in semitones \; pmod 0-1: portamento mode (full time) \; port 0-99: portamento time \; fcv 0-99: foot controller volume \; sus 0-1: sustain on / off \; pon 0-1: portamento on / off \; chor 0-1: chorus (set 0) \; mwp 0-99: mod wheel pitch \; mwa 0-99: mod wheel amplitude \; bcp 0-99: breath control pitch \; bca 0-99: breath control amplitude \; bcpb 0-99: breath control pitch bias (50 = centre) \; bceb 0-99: breath control EG bias \; rev 0-7: reverb rate (0 = off \, 7 = fast) \; fcp 0-99: foot controller pitch \; fca 0-99: foot controller amplitude \;   \; Operators: name + operator number 1-4 \, e.g. ar1 \, osw4: \; ar1-ar4 0-31: attack rate \; d1r1-d1r4 0-31: decay 1 rate \; d2r1-d2r4 0-31: decay 2 rate \; rr1-rr4 0-15: release rate \; d1l1-d1l4 0-15: decay 1 level \; ls1-ls4 0-99: level scaling \; rs1-rs4 0-3: rate scaling \; ebs1-ebs4 0-7: EG bias sensitivity \; ame1-ame4 0-1: amplitude modulation on / off \; kvs1-kvs4 0-7: key velocity sensitivity \; out1-out4 0-99: output level \; crs1-crs4 0-63: frequency coarse \; det1-det4 0-6: detune (3 = centre) \; fix1-fix4 0-1: fixed frequency (0 ratio \, 1 fixed) \; fixr1-fixr4 0-7: fixed range 250 Hz ... 32 kHz \; fin1-fin4 0-15: frequency fine \; osw1-osw4 0-7: waveform W1-W8 (0-7) \; sh1-sh4 0-3: EG shift: 0 96 dB \, 1 48 \, 2 24 \, 3 12, f 64;
#X obj 60 3622 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Firmware\ and\ battery\ RAM 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3650 Arguments: [tx81z~ <firmware> <battery RAM file>] \, paths relative to the patch. The firmware (64 KB \, e.g. tx81z-v1.6.bin from the MAME set tx81z) is not included. The battery RAM file keeps voices \, performances and the system setup. If it does not exist \, tx81z~ runs the factory init (about 26 s of DSP time \, it runs only while DSP is on): test mode loads the presets into the internal memory \, then the front panel sets MIDI Control: receive omni \, program change \, control change \, pitch bend and Exclusive on. Without Exclusive on the firmware ignores all SysEx \, so parameter changes and the editor would not work. Then it saves the file., f 64;
#X obj 60 3854 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Program\ change 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3882 The TX81Z selects I01-C32 with program changes 0-127 (I 0-31 \, A 32-63 \, B 64-95 \, C 96-127). Bank D only via its program change table. Program changes need the program change switch on (the factory init sets it \, or pcswitch 1). After every voice change the firmware sends its voice dump: tx81z~ reads it \, the editor and the controller follow., f 64;
